# Allowlist for Vercel deployments: ship ONLY what the serverless functions
# (api/*) and the dashboard need at runtime. Everything a user commits to their
# own repo stays OUT of the public deployment — cv.md, config/profile.yml,
# bullet-bank.md, story-bank.md, article-digest.md, CLAUDE.md, data/* (the
# dashboard writes these back to the repo via "Save to my repo"),
# linkedin-research/*, and any .env* file.
#
# Vercel bundles each function from the UPLOADED fileset, so anything a function
# imports at runtime MUST be re-included below or the function breaks. The
# included set was derived by tracing every transitive import of api/*.js.
#
# Uses git's anchored "/*" allowlist form (see gitignore docs): a bare "*"
# matches at every depth and would re-exclude files inside re-included dirs, so
# each level is handled explicitly.

# 1. Ignore every top-level entry.
/*

# 2. Ship the api directory in full — every file under it is needed.
!/api

# 3. lib: ONLY the modules imported by api/*.js. ssrf.mjs is scanner-only (never
#    reached from an api function), so it is left out. Re-include the dir,
#    re-exclude its contents, then add back the traced files.
!/lib
/lib/*
!/lib/atsDetect.js
!/lib/bulletBank.mjs
!/lib/auth.mjs
!/lib/github.js
!/lib/memory.mjs
!/lib/portalsMeta.mjs
!/lib/resumeParse.mjs
!/lib/writingRules.mjs

# 4. scanner: ONLY the modules imported by api/*.js at runtime.
!/scanner
/scanner/*
!/scanner/applicationPackage.mjs
!/scanner/config.mjs
!/scanner/enrich.mjs
!/scanner/evaluate.mjs
!/scanner/html.mjs
!/scanner/interviewPackage.mjs

# 5. Ship the dashboard.
!/dashboard

# 6. Ship the manifests and the Vercel config.
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/vercel.json
